## Findings — store 99 (all fixed)

**1. Restroom block interior was walkable floor** — `(601.7, 675.7)–(670.7, 719.7)`
Crop `walkable_overlay` 3×3 cell (2,1), confirmed by a 300-dpi mask render of pt 480–700 × 650–740 and a 2-pt line scan: rows y=688…718 are reachable at x 602-606, 630-634, 638-640, 664-668 — the open floor on both sides of the T-partition stem, i.e. both toilet-room interiors plus the vestibule. Bay is walled at x=601.7/670.7, entered through one 29-pt mouth at (620.8–650.1, y=674), split by the drawn T (bar y=683.7–685.9, stem x=636.2–638.4). No fixture, no product label, no frontage inside. Truth: enclosed room, not sales floor (cf. 24 `Restrooms interior`, 660 `restroom vestibule…(enclosed room)`, 658 restroom block exclusion). **Fix: exclusion rect** `[601,675,671,721]`. The `RESTROOMS` anchor at (637.3,665.4) is north of the mouth and still snaps to alley floor.

**2. Tobacco kiosk back room was walkable** — `(551, 676)–(598, 720)`, 19 m²
Same mask render; the line scan shows its **only** link to the alley is a 4-pt slit at x=594–598, y=674 between the counter's east end and the restroom wall — 0.4 m, not a customer corridor. The bay is walled west (x=551) and roofed by the counter wall x=551–588, with the sawtooth-faced Tobacco fixture `[551.4,667,593.4,676]` standing on it facing **north** into the alley. Empty walled floor behind a service counter = staff (cf. 265/269/811). Also confirmed by the "green floor >2.6 m from any printed text" scan, which listed it as a 10.8 m² textless cluster at centroid (574,706). **Fix: exclusion rect** `[550,674,600,721]`.

**3. Meal Simple frontage corridor sealed — the store-24 failure mode** — `x 474–536, y 582–604`
Culled pocket #327 "near AISLE 15" at centroid (508,589). The 22-pt (2.1 m) shopping aisle between the upper case `[446,559,532,581]` and the middle case `[474,605,524,611]` is green for its west 32 pt and white from x=474 east — green at its mouth, white deeper in. The department's own printed name `Meal Simple` (450–524, 583–596) sits on the sealed half; the dense label probe measured `'Simple'` at 2.29 m from reachable floor. Cause: the derived `auto:CHECKSTANDS` rect `[439.5,501.5,861.2,605.1]` carries the looser 20-pt lane bridge, which closes a 22-pt corridor wherever it overlaps. The parallel corridor south of the middle case (y=612–622) survived and shows what this one should look like. **Fix: inclusion rect** `[472,582,540,606]`. `'Simple'` now drops off the >1.6 m list entirely.

**4. Cooking Connection demo-counter interior was walkable** — inner chain `(258.4,321.1) (276.8,337.8) (277.2,348.3) (265.0,361.7) (254.1,362.5) (236.4,346.5)`
**5. Sushiya sushi-bar interior was walkable** — inner chain `(333.6,406.9) (352.0,423.6) (352.4,434.1) (340.2,447.5) (329.4,448.3) (311.7,432.3)`
Mask render of pt 195–400 × 300–470, plus point probes. Staff work inside these horseshoes; the pipeline can never condemn them, because the mouths (41 pt / ~3.9 m) are far wider than any seal bridge **and** neither "Sushiya" nor "Cooking Connection" is in `extract.py`'s anchor vocabulary, so no seal disk and no VERIFY ever forms — the same reason 24 and 660 hand-excluded the identical fixtures. **Fix: two poly exclusions** traced from the fixtures' own inner vertex chains (`fixture_polys[174]`/`[173]`), closed across the mouth.

**6. walk_truth was inadequate and one point was mislabelled**
- `[598,275,"Meat department frontage"]` — there is no Meat department on this map. The `MEAT` anchor is `extract.py` reading the vertical shelf label *"Beans (Canned)/Canned Vegetables/Tomatoes/Chili/Fish/Meat"* printed inside the aisle-5 corridor. Relabelled to what the point actually is.
- 12 must / 8 must_not for a 37-aisle store: no point anywhere in aisles 14–21 (Healthy Living, Greeting Cards, Toys/Seasonal), none in aisles 23/27/30/34/37 (only aisle 25 covered the whole east wing), none for Market/Beer-Wine/Blooms/Meal Simple/Cafe/Sushiya/Cooking-Connection frontage or the east perimeter aisle; no must_not for restrooms, Tobacco, Business Center, any of the three lease rooms, the Deli or Bakery block, or the west back-of-house band.
**Fix: rewritten walk_truth — 35 must / 27 must_not**, every coordinate probed. Each of the five defects above now has a point that would have caught it. The 10 must_not points that sit on structurally-open floor (Seafood, west band, both horseshoes, Pharmacy, Admin, Business Center, 3 lease rooms, both lanes) are real sealing guards; the restroom/Tobacco points were moved off the pictogram ink onto open floor (604,700)/(666,700) for the same reason.

