2. **Aisle 2 corridor at "Kitchen Gadgets"** `rect [493, 106, 520, 331]` — the lone VERIFY. `extract.py` turned the printed product-category label *Kitchen Gadgets* into a `KITCHEN` anchor (which is in `SERVICE_DEPTS`), but this store has no kitchen service counter: the label sits in the open corridor between gondolas x=484.3–492.9 and x=520.3–528.8, with the AISLE 2 badge directly below at (509, 334). Legitimate customer space → inclusion.

No `exclusions.json`, `zones.json` or `seal_zones.json` needed — zones and seal zones derived correctly.

**`data/99/walk_truth.json`** — 12 `must` / 8 `must_not`, all read off the overlay and `geometry.json` and each verified to sit inside the feature it names: front action alley, SW entrance approach, Produce/Seafood/Bakery/Dairy/Pharmacy/Meat frontages, aisles 2/8/25, the reopened Card & Party aisle; against page corner, the Texas Backyard lot and SE cart corral (both outside the boundary), the two label-identified staff areas (Seafood wedge interior 176,418 and Pharmacy room 1080,580), Lease Space, Admin office, and a checkout-lane interior.

