data/99/qa/audit.log:12:Culled pocket #327 "near AISLE 15" at centroid (508,589). The 22-pt (2.1 m) shopping aisle between the upper case `[446,559,532,581]` and the middle case `[474,605,524,611]` is green for its west 32 pt and white from x=474 east — green at its mouth, white deeper in. The department's own printed name `Meal Simple` (450–524, 583–596) sits on the sealed half; the dense label probe measured `'Simple'` at 2.29 m from reachable floor. Cause: the derived `auto:CHECKSTANDS` rect `[439.5,501.5,861.2,605.1]` carries the looser 20-pt lane bridge, which closes a 22-pt corridor wherever it overlaps. The parallel corridor south of the middle case (y=612–622) survived and shows what this one should look like. **Fix: inclusion rect** `[472,582,540,606]`. `'Simple'` now drops off the >1.6 m list entirely.
data/99/qa/audit.log:19:- `[598,275,"Meat department frontage"]` — there is no Meat department on this map. The `MEAT` anchor is `extract.py` reading the vertical shelf label *"Beans (Canned)/Canned Vegetables/Tomatoes/Chili/Fish/Meat"* printed inside the aisle-5 corridor. Relabelled to what the point actually is.
